{
	title: 'Web uses locally bundled IBM Plex Mono Regular',
	spec: 'The main web UI uses locally served IBM Plex Mono, with Regular 400 and Bold 700 as the tracked defaults and corresponding italic faces. WOFF2 binaries are not tracked; /src/web/fonts/*.woff2 is gitignored. scripts/fonts downloads the four default faces from IBM/plex master packages/plex-mono/fonts/complete/woff2, or selected known face names supplied as arguments, and preserves existing files if downloads fail. Run bash scripts/fonts before starting a fresh checkout. The upstream SIL Open Font License remains tracked in src/web/fonts/OFL.txt. Same-origin font routes serve known face names as font/woff2 with caching. There are no third-party browser font requests or automatic network downloads. Body, controls and Markdown code share the family; terminal fonts stay unchanged. Experimental weights and italic alternatives remain local until selected.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Assets downloaded unmodified from IBM/plex master, packages/plex-mono/fonts/complete/woff2, with the repository LICENSE.txt. All four same-origin routes returned HTTP 200, font/woff2 and wOF2 signatures. Focused web suite had 17 passes and 36 failures: a host-mode event expectation mismatch and Chromium startup timeouts prevented browser verification.'
